# Multi-tenant dashboard configuration.
#
# One deployment serves several people. Each logs in with their own password
# and sees only their own Supabase project. The password ALONE identifies who
# you are — there is no name picker, because that would publish the roster of
# who uses this dashboard on an unauthenticated page.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Session signing key — REQUIRED once more than one person is configured.
# Generate with:  openssl rand -hex 32
#
# This signs the session cookie, which carries WHICH person you are. It must
# not be any user's password: whoever knows the signing key can mint a cookie
# naming any persona. Set this BEFORE adding a second person.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SESSION_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# One block per person. The _PASSWORD variable is what defines a persona —
# the app discovers people by scanning for PERSONA_*_PASSWORD at runtime, so
# ADDING A FOURTH PERSON IS JUST THREE MORE VARIABLES AND A REDEPLOY. No code
# change, no list to keep in sync.
#
# Passwords double as identity, so they must be UNIQUE and high-entropy.
# Generate each with:  openssl rand -base64 24
# (If two people share a password, neither can log in — the app refuses to
# guess rather than handing one person the other's data.)
#
# SUPABASE_URL is the BASE project URL, no trailing path. The Supabase Data
# API page shows it with "/rest/v1/" appended — strip that.
# SERVICE_KEY is the SECRET key (sb_secret_...), not the publishable one.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PERSONA_OWNER_LABEL=Ifiok
PERSONA_OWNER_PASSWORD=
PERSONA_OWNER_SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxx.supabase.co
PERSONA_OWNER_SERVICE_KEY=sb_secret_...

PERSONA_BEYONCE_LABEL=Beyonce
PERSONA_BEYONCE_PASSWORD=
PERSONA_BEYONCE_SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxx.supabase.co
PERSONA_BEYONCE_SERVICE_KEY=sb_secret_...

PERSONA_HASSAN_LABEL=Hassan
PERSONA_HASSAN_PASSWORD=
PERSONA_HASSAN_SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxx.supabase.co
PERSONA_HASSAN_SERVICE_KEY=sb_secret_...

# Optional: restrict which discovered personas are active, without deleting
# their credentials. Leave unset normally.
# PERSONA_IDS=owner,beyonce,hassan

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Legacy single-tenant vars. Used ONLY when no PERSONA_* config exists, so
# this code can deploy to the existing project unchanged. Delete once every
# deployment has SESSION_SECRET + PERSONA_* set.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY is no longer needed at all — the browser no
# longer talks to Supabase directly (realtime was replaced with polling).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DASHBOARD_PASSWORD=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY=
